       "type": "text",
       "html": "<p>The SIE divides trading activity into four conceptual \"markets.\" Memorize what each one means — this is a high-yield, frequently confused topic.</p><ul><li><strong>First Market:</strong> Trading of <strong>exchange-listed securities ON an exchange</strong> (e.g., an NYSE-listed stock traded on the NYSE floor).</li><li><strong>Second Market:</strong> Trading of <strong>unlisted (OTC) securities</strong> — securities not listed on an exchange, traded over the counter.</li><li><strong>Third Market:</strong> Trading of <strong>exchange-listed securities in the OTC market</strong> (a listed stock traded OTC, often by an institution through a market maker, away from the exchange floor).</li><li><strong>Fourth Market:</strong> <strong>Direct trading between institutions</strong> with no broker-dealer intermediary, typically through ECNs (institution-to-institution).</li></ul>"
