   "summary": "Investment companies pool investor money into professionally managed, diversified portfolios. This chapter covers the three types defined by the Investment Company Act of 1940 — open-end (mutual) funds, closed-end funds, and unit investment trusts — plus NAV and forward pricing, sales charges, share classes, breakpoints, 12b-1 fees, fund management structure, and the rules governing redemption.",
