       "type": "text",
       "html": "<p><strong>Moneyness</strong> describes the relationship between the stock's market price and the option's strike price. It tells you whether exercising would produce value. The rule flips between calls and puts because a call holder wants to buy low and a put holder wants to sell high.</p>"
