       "html": "<p>A <strong>Real Estate Investment Trust (REIT)</strong> is a company that pools investor capital to own, operate, or finance income-producing real estate. REITs let ordinary investors gain real-estate exposure with the liquidity and diversification of a pooled security. A REIT is <em>not</em> an investment company under the Investment Company Act of 1940 and is <em>not</em> a direct participation program — a frequent exam trap. Unlike a DPP, a REIT does <strong>not</strong> pass through losses to investors; only income is passed through.</p>"
